WEBVTT

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:05.288
And so if we're going to use mRNA
as a therapeutic,

00:02:05.329 --> 00:02:06.497
it needs our help.

00:02:07.123 --> 00:02:10.626
It needs protection,
and it needs to be told where to go.

00:02:11.919 --> 00:02:13.254
And that's where I come in.

00:02:14.255 --> 00:02:18.593
For over five decades,
scientists and engineers like myself

00:02:18.593 --> 00:02:22.889
have been creating the shipping materials
for nucleic acid drugs,

00:02:22.889 --> 00:02:25.308
like DNA and RNA.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:29.645
Through trial and error,
we've created packages

00:02:29.687 --> 00:02:33.399
that deliver intact vases
to the wrong address;